{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1139333-a-thing-opened-heart","id":1139333,"title":"[A Thing] Opened Heart","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-10T19:29:29-07:00","id":1139333,"title":"[A Thing] Opened Heart","content":"Most of the world is spiritually deaf, walled off in their little prisons of meat and bone. Empathy is rare - it hurts to reach out to others. The world hates it, after all.<br /> <br /> The powers that be care nothing for your happiness, or whether or not you understand your fellows. Hell, in many cases, they <i>like</i> that you aren't making friends with everyone. They want to keep the world cold and tied down. They want people to bury their heads in the sand. They want the world to be a prison of misery and fear, where everyone looks out for themselves and no one else.<br /> <br /> To <i>hell</i> with that. Hold your head high, and lift those around you up onto your shoulders.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Opened Heart (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) [Supernatural]</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Empathy \u2022\u2022, Integrity<br /> <br /> <b>Effects:</b> Your heart is open to those around you - anyone that so much as <i>looks</i> at you gets a general sense of your current Aspirations. If you have the four-dot version of this merit, you may spend reflexively spend one Willpower while speaking to another character to learn their current Aspirations.<br /> <br /> More impressively, you are masterful at helping people deal with their emotions. Whenever another character suffers a Breaking Point in your presence and you support them emotionally, they may add your Empathy to their Integrity for the purposes of that roll. Additionally, anyone who spends a scene peacefully chatting with you may choose to resolve a Condition that could be resolved by gaining or losing a dot of Integrity.<br /> <br /> The four-dot version of this merit allows you to make someone a deal - by openly discussing your goals and dreams with someone else, you may offer to mutually support each-other in your goals. If your counterpart accepts, you each choose one of each-other's Aspirations, and gain an Aspiration to help the other character achieve that goal. As long as you are in the same scene with each-other, both of you may spend Willpower on actions the other takes that are related to the shared Aspirations.<br /> <br /> <b>Special:</b> Characters with this merit may purchase the True Friend merit for 1xp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T19:46:05-07:00","id":1139336,"title":"","content":"For those of you expecting more explicit drawbacks:<br /> <br /> 1) Letting people know your Aspirations gives them a <i>lot</i> of power if they're trying to manipulate you. Plus, you can't hide what you want, which can get messy if that thing is &quot;I want to kill Molly the Mage&quot;.<br /> <br /> 2) Breaking Points for Integrity are <i>supposed</i> to be player-driven and player-determined. By taking this merit, you're expressing interest in playing someone who is emotionally open - calling for a few more Breaking Points seems appropriate (<i>and</i> gives you Beats indirectly).<br /> <br /> 3) The cool perks it gives you require that you spend time around people who are putting themselves through mental and emotional trauma. They don't give <i>you</i> any kind of personal protection from the horrors you see and that will (probably) be described to you.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Oh, and a note about the Aspiration sharing. This has a few wide reaching consequences:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The other guy <i>wants to help you</i>. You have a pair of shared goals - this goes deeper than just &quot;yeah, sure, I'll help you out&quot;.<br /> \u2022 It has knock-on effects on Social Maneuvering - you can convince each-other to do things more easily, and people trying to get you to betray each-other will run into problems.<br /> \u2022 You can get Beats from helping each-other out.<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind that Aspirations are your goals <i>as the player</i>, not <i>as the character</i>. It's valid to have Aspirations like &quot;fall in love with so-and-so&quot; or &quot;fall back off the wagon&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T04:19:50-07:00","id":1139870,"title":"","content":"Awesome work man good job","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13426,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","user":"Ameraaaaaa","date":". 09-15-2017, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T05:34:25-07:00","id":1140134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whenever another character suffers a Breaking Point in your presence and you support them emotionally, they may add your Empathy to their Integrity for the purposes of that roll. </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't that be &quot;add your Empathy to their Resolve + Composure for the Breaking Point roll&quot;?<br /> <br /> Otherwise, excellent work! Reminds me of that True Friendship Supernatural Style you wrote.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Do you think a non-human entity could have this Merit as a Numen if they were sufficiently human-like? I am thinking about giving this to one of my NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-14-2017, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T18:22:03-07:00","id":1140941,"title":"","content":"I went with boosting Integrity for aesthetic reasons - you aren't boosting their mental state, you're boosting their emotional fortitude (if that makes sense).<br /> <br /> And this actually dovetails into the True Friendship merit - there's a reason it gives you a discount on True Friend.<br /> <br /> My gut says no to the Numen thing - it doesn't feel right for a Spirit to be that sympatico, you know?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T18:51:31-07:00","id":1140948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1139333-a-thing-opened-heart?p=1140941#post1140941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I went with boosting Integrity for aesthetic reasons - you aren't boosting their mental state, you're boosting their emotional fortitude (if that makes sense).<br /> <br /> And this actually dovetails into the True Friendship merit - there's a reason it gives you a discount on True Friend.<br /> <br /> My gut says no to the Numen thing - it doesn't feel right for a Spirit to be that sympatico, you know?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, understood. The NPC I am talking about is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1120200-new-horror-little-morpheus\"><b>this one.</b></a> I envision him as pretty sympatico. You would not mind if I added Opened Heart 4 to his sheet despite what your gut says, right?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T21:06:33-07:00","id":1140970,"title":"","content":"The description for Little Morpheus makes me feel that it's <i>very much</i> not an appropriate choice - I'm coming away with the impression of a high-functioning sociopath with good intentions.<br /> <br /> But if you want to, I can do nothing to stop you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}